This is not the place to attempt a summary of all the things Jim Crapu-
chettes' FUTIL program can do.  For that you should get a copy of the
OS/8 'device extension kit' release notes or the OS/278 manual.

The .FUtil command implemented by CCLX has the following options:

		.FUtil	[dev:filename]  /E  /L  /S  /O=nnnn

The options specify in order: short Error messages, Load mode (.ex=.LD)
Save mode (.ex=.SV), and Offset mode (null .ex).  For the latter 'nnnn'
is the 12-bit offset.
